Wrong (A): A voluntary change in accounting principle uses retrospective application, not restatement. The terminology distinction matters for proper classification.
Wrong (B): Mandatory changes required by a new ASU also use retrospective application, not the term restatement.
Wrong (D): Changes in accounting estimate are applied prospectively under ASC 250, not through restatement.$EXPL$
