-- Q11703: Contingencies [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 740-10-25, uncertain tax positions use a specific two-step framework that supersedes ASC 450 for income tax contingencies. Step 1 applies a more-likely-than-not (>50%) recognition threshold. Step 2 measures the benefit at the largest amount with >50% cumulative probability of realization.
Wrong (A): ASC 450 does not apply to income tax contingencies. ASC 740-10 provides a separate, specialized framework for uncertain tax positions.
Wrong (B): Disclosure-only treatment under ASC 450 is also incorrect because the ASC 740 framework, not ASC 450, governs tax uncertainties.
Wrong (C): Meeting the recognition threshold does not mean the full benefit is recognized. Step 2 measurement may result in only partial benefit recognition based on cumulative probability analysis.$EXPL$
